 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Their claim (183:3-14) gets no motif; the gloss after it is «أنتم كاذبون في قولكم». No fire for the burnt offering, nothing literal for the Fire or Paradise (185). A scroll and a lamp for the scriptures and the illuminating Book, an hourglass for death, a leaf for the deceiving enjoyment, coins for trials in wealth, a mountain for patience. STAGING v4: 183-184: the group from the People of the Book voices its claim when called to Islam (the gloss frames it: هؤلاء اليهود حين دعوا إلى الإسلام) and shakes heads on the refusal to believe; no fire, no offering and no killing drawn; nothing on «قل» or the messengers (184:5); the earlier scriptures as scroll and lamp plates. 185 stays ambient: death, the Day, the Fire and Paradise. 186: in a market the believers give to a poor man on «أموالكم» (both tafsirs: النفقات الواجبة والمستحبة), then the People of the Book and the polytheists (dark robes) speak and point at them: the abuse they will hear; patience only as the mountain plate and the camera on the believers (the patience is conditional). No wounds or killing drawn."
 },
